<com.aptare.sc.dal.versioning.ObjectMap>
  <version>2</version>
  <className>com.aptare.sc.domain.reportTemplateDesigner.RtdTemplate</className>
  <data>
    <entry>
      <string>longDescription</string>
      <string>Select date range and one or more backup clients in the scope. &#xd;
If two copies of a original backup exist, the blue bar would be a height of one (since the 2nd Duplication Copy is one extra copy) and Yellow bar would be at the height of 50 % indicating the percentage of extra backup copies. The same situation for three copies would be a blue bar height of two and a yellow bar indicating percentage of 67 %.In addition, users can drilldown from the bar for a specific date to obtain complete details of all the NetBackup duplication backup copies.</string>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>reportVersion</string>
      <string>1.0</string>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>isCloudTemplate</string>
      <boolean>false</boolean>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>inventoryType</string>
      <list>
        <long>0</long>
      </list>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>reportGuid</string>
      <string>5ec403ee-7aa3-440d-b05e-eafe2c784bb2</string>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>inventoryCategory</string>
      <long>0</long>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>description</string>
      <string>This is a report that tries to mimic the &quot;Duplicate Copies&quot; Report in NetBackup OpsCenter. The report is used by OpsCenter users to ensure there is more than 1 Duplication copy (also known as extra copy) of the Original Backup for Backup Client/Clients. </string>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>exportName</string>
      <string>NetBackup Duplicate Copies</string>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>version</string>
      <double>0.0</double>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>products</string>
      <list/>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <string>reportDefinition</string>
      <com.aptare.sc.dal.versioning.ObjectMap>
        <version>1</version>
        <className>com.aptare.sc.domain.report.ReportDefinition</className>
        <data>
          <entry>
            <string>drilldown</string>
            <boolean>false</boolean>
          </entry>
          <entry>
            <string>designerComponents</string>
            <list>
              <com.aptare.sc.domain.reportDesigner.ReportDesignerComponent>
                <name>timePeriod</name>
                <componentScript>
                  <before/>
                  <after/>
                </componentScript>
                <referenceData/>
              </com.aptare.sc.domain.reportDesigner.ReportDesignerComponent>
              <com.aptare.sc.domain.reportDesigner.ReportDesignerComponent>
                <name>scope</name>
                <componentScript>
                  <before/>
                  <after/>
                </componentScript>
                <configuration>
